<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:64:default">
<!--
    kuna relocatable-object loader: a MIPS relocation may be one operation of
    a longer expression. GNU as writes `%hi(%neg(%gp_rel(f)))` in an N32
    object as three records at one offset, GPREL16, SUB and HI16, each taking
    the result of the one before; an N64 record packs up to three operations
    and an expression may continue into the next record at the same offset.
    The loader applied each N32 record on its own and each N64 record alone,
    so every N32 .cpsetup left $gp at the function's entry and its GOT reads
    landed below .text (`*dat_3f8080`), and a call through a composed
    expression kept its placeholder (sub_0, halt_baddata, trap).

    Stage: P1 program prep (relocatable-object loader); a strict loader fix,
    no option. Single pass.

    Images: tests/fixtures/octeon-relocations/pic-gcc73-n32.o (GCC 7.3 N32 PIC,
    pic.c) and call-composed-{n32,64}-be.o (call-composed.S); see that
    directory's README and provenance files.

    Assert #1: N32 PIC read_global reads global_value through the GOT.
    Assert #2: N32 PIC call_external calls external through the GOT.
    Assert #3: every composed N32 and N64 call names its callee.
    Assert #4: no call is left at a placeholder or bad instruction.
    Assert #5: same-offset N32 REL words accumulate both symbols in BE/LE.
    Assert #6: implicit addends are reread with 32-bit wrapping in BE/LE.
    Assert #7: composed PC32 wraps an unsigned R32 result in N32/N64 BE/LE.
    Assert #8: standalone PC32 wraps a displacement below the signed range.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">03e0000800000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
